  "result": "The file is `src/server/jobs/webhook-delivery-job.ts`. The messages a customer's server receives are outgoing webhook deliveries, and this job is what retries them:\n\n- **Attempts allowed:** `const MAX_ATTEMPTS = 6` (line 22). Once `delivery.attempts > MAX_ATTEMPTS`, the delivery is marked failed for good with the log message \"giving up after N attempts\".\n- **How the wait grows:** `backoffMs(attempts)` (lines 90–92) returns `Math.min(300_000, 2 ** (attempts - 1) * 1_000)`. The wait doubles each time (1s, 2s, 4s…) up to a limit of five minutes. On attempt 0 it retries straight away.\n\nTwo other places look related but aren't the source:\n- `src/config/constants.ts` defines `WEBHOOK_MAX_ATTEMPTS = 5`, but nothing uses it. The job uses its own value of 6.\n- `src/server/jobs/queue.ts` has a separate `MAX_ATTEMPTS = 5` and `backoffMs` (capped at 60s). Those apply to the general job queue, not to webhook deliveries.\n\nANSWER: src/server/jobs/webhook-delivery-job.ts",
